 ### JRFC-0003.2 Structured logs
 Services MUST emit logs as structured key-value records through the shared logger, not
 as interpolated free-text strings built by concatenation.
 
-- Applies when: the content adds or changes a log call.
-- Not applies when: the content only changes logger configuration.
+- Applies when: service code adds or changes a log call.
+- Not applies when: the content only changes logger configuration, or the code is a command-line tool, script, benchmark or local developer tool, not a service.
 - Enforcement: agent
 
